==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipAccessControl  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipAccessControl.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to construct an Operation where a non-owner member performs OpPatchTask or OpDeleteTask on a task they do not own. This directly violates FR-008/FR-009 and the OwnershipBasedAccess predicate, which requires that every such operation be performed by the owner or an admin.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_009_MemberOwnerOnly, LeastPrivilege
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_008_009_MemberOwnerOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact dissolves the one-to-one binding between Operations and AuditEntries. The injected violation creates two Operations both claiming the same AuditEntry, which simulates a 'reuse/rewrite' of an audit record — exactly the mutation that the append-only invariant forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditImmutable, AuditCompleteness
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model place an Operation that targets a task whose team differs from the operation's team. The injection explicitly constructs such a cross-team access, violating the byte-equivalent 404 isolation invariant central to FR-014 and SC-004.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_014_CrossTeamIsolation
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_014_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the requirement that PostTask and DeleteTask operations produce exactly one audit entry. The injection creates a PostTask operation with no associated audit entry, modelling the SC-007 failure mode where a task change has no corresponding audit trail entry.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerEditEvent, AppendOnly
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerEditEvent: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_TeamMembershipUnique  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_TeamMembershipUnique.als
    rationale: Removing the composite-PK uniqueness constraint allows a user to hold two different roles in the same team simultaneously. The injection creates exactly this scenario, which would let a member claim admin privileges in the same team — violating the per-team single-role invariant of FR-007.
    expected to FAIL: FR_007_PerTeamRole, AuthRequiredEverywhere, AttributionCorrectness
      - FR_007_PerTeamRole: FAIL (expected)
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AssigneeIsMember  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AssigneeIsMember.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a task to carry an assignee who is not a member of the task's team. The injection creates a task whose assignee belongs to a different team, directly violating the FR-012 same-team-assignee constraint and the ValidationBeforeMutation predicate.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_AssigneeTeamMember, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - FR_012_AssigneeTeamMember: PASS (vacuous?)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: PASS (vacuous?)

